    dcterm:created "2018-01-16T16:13:52.465000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:description "[RawPOS](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0169) is a point-of-sale (POS) malware family that searches for cardholder data on victims. It has been in use since at least 2008. FireEye divides RawPOS into three components: FIENDCRY, DUEBREW, and DRIFTWOOD." ;
