<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/attack/software/S0023> a attack:Malware ;
    dcterm:created "2017-05-31T21:32:19.389000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:description "[CHOPSTICK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0023) is a malware family of modular backdoors used by [APT28](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0007). It has been used since at least 2012 and is usually dropped on victims as second-stage malware, though it has been used as first-stage malware in several cases. It has both Windows and Linux variants. It is tracked separately from the [X-Agent for Android](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0314)." ;
    dcterm:identifier "S0023" ;
    dcterm:modified "2023-03-26T17:51:20.403000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
