<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/attack/software/S0377> a attack:Malware ;
    dcterm:created "2019-04-19T16:40:24.922000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:description "[Ebury](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0377) is an OpenSSH backdoor and credential stealer targeting Linux servers and container hosts developed by [Windigo](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0124). [Ebury](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0377) is primarily installed through modifying shared libraries (`.so` files) executed by the legitimate OpenSSH program. First seen in 2009, [Ebury](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0377) has been used to maintain a botnet of servers, deploy additional malware, and steal cryptocurrency wallets, credentials, and credit card details." ;
    dcterm:identifier "S0377" ;
    dcterm:modified "2024-09-20T21:15:51.302000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:title "Ebury" ;
