<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/attack/technique/T1115> a attack:Technique ;
    dcterm:created "2017-05-31T21:31:25.967000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:description """Adversaries may collect data stored in the clipboard from users copying information within or between applications. 

For example, on Windows adversaries can access clipboard data by using <code>clip.exe</code> or <code>Get-Clipboard</code>. Additionally, adversaries may monitor then replace users’ clipboard with their data (e.g., [Transmitted Data Manipulation](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1565/002)).

macOS and Linux also have commands, such as <code>pbpaste</code>, to grab clipboard contents.""" ;
    dcterm:identifier "T1115" ;
    dcterm:modified "2023-04-14T21:51:47.277000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:title "Clipboard Data" ;
