<http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/attack/technique/T1518> a attack:Technique ;
    dcterm:created "2019-09-16T17:52:44.147000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:description """Adversaries may attempt to get a listing of software and software versions that are installed on a system or in a cloud environment. Adversaries may use the information from [Software Discovery](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1518) during automated discovery to shape follow-on behaviors, including whether or not the adversary fully infects the target and/or attempts specific actions.

Such software may be deployed widely across the environment for configuration management or security reasons, such as [Software Deployment Tools](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1072), and may allow adversaries broad access to infect devices or move laterally.

Adversaries may attempt to enumerate software for a variety of reasons, such as figuring out what security measures are present or if the compromised system has a version of software that is vulnerable to [Exploitation for Privilege Escalation](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1068).""" ;
    dcterm:identifier "T1518" ;
    dcterm:modified "2024-04-16T00:16:06.689000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterm:title "Software Discovery" ;
    attack:accomplishesTactic <http://w3id.org/sepses/resource/attack/tactic/TA0007> ;
